{%- doc -%}
  Echoes the 1-based position of the product option that holds sizes, or nothing when there is
  no match. The option is identified by the global `settings.size_option_name` theme setting.

  Two consumers rely on this, which is why the lookup is shared rather than duplicated:
  `snippets/variant-main-picker.liquid` (to place the size-guide link beside the right option)
  and `blocks/return-policy-acknowledgment.liquid` (to record the confirmed size on the
  line-item property). A theme block cannot read another block's settings, so a block-level
  setting would mean two sources of truth that drift apart silently; one global setting keeps
  them honest.

  Emits nothing when `settings.size_option_name` is blank, which is the intended kill switch:
  no size-guide link anywhere, and the acknowledgement falls back to the variant title.

  Callers must strip the captured value before comparing it numerically. This snippet already
  avoids emitting whitespace, but `{% capture %}` preserves whatever surrounds the render tag.

  @param {object} product_resource - The product whose options are searched.

  @example
  {%- capture size_position %}{% render 'size-option-position', product_resource: product %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- assign size_position = size_position | strip -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign target = settings.size_option_name | downcase | strip

  if target != blank
    for product_option in product_resource.options_with_values
      assign option_name = product_option.name | downcase | strip
      if option_name == target
        echo product_option.position
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
